WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:04:08.649
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
04:08.919 --> 04:10.360
It's—it's recording now?

3
04:10.879 --> 04:11.479
Yeah, it's recording.

4
04:11.479 --> 04:12.120
Cao Jun.

5
04:13.039 --> 04:13.360
Well...

6
04:13.360 --> 04:14.800
How about I drive a lap for you?

7
04:14.840 --> 04:15.639
No need, no need.

8
04:15.879 --> 04:16.759
Just stay seated.

9
04:17.079 --> 04:17.560
All right.

10
04:19.680 --> 04:21.279
Your plant had a drinking contest yesterday.

11
04:21.319 --> 04:22.240
How come you didn't go?

12
04:23.399 --> 04:24.279
I'm no good at drinking.

13
04:24.319 --> 04:25.279
Didn't dare join the crowd.

14
04:25.600 --> 04:26.560
They wouldn't care for me anyway.

15
04:27.000 --> 04:28.519
People at breweries usually drink a lot, don't they?

16
04:28.959 --> 04:29.519
Yeah.

17
04:29.839 --> 04:31.639
There sure are plenty of heavy drinkers here.

18
04:31.639 --> 04:32.839
But two departments can't drink.

19
04:33.279 --> 04:34.240
One is Quality Inspection.

20
04:34.240 --> 04:35.079
Sister Xuemei's department.

21
04:35.360 --> 04:36.959
The other is us drivers.

22
04:37.199 --> 04:37.759
We can't drink.

23
04:38.160 --> 04:39.600
Don't you drive a forklift?

24
04:40.160 --> 04:40.480
Well...

25
04:40.959 --> 04:42.199
A forklift is still a vehicle.

26
04:42.399 --> 04:44.120
A forklift driver is still a driver.

27
04:44.439 --> 04:45.000
Drivers don't drink.

28
04:45.000 --> 04:45.720
That keeps us out of trouble.

29
04:45.920 --> 04:46.360
Right?

30
04:46.560 --> 04:47.279
Right, right, right.

31
04:51.319 --> 04:52.160
Hey, Reporter Shen...

32
04:52.199 --> 04:53.519
Could you, uh, turn this off first?

33
04:53.839 --> 04:54.439
Turn it off for a second.

34
04:54.639 --> 04:55.319
Saves battery, saves battery.

35
04:55.319 --> 04:56.160
I—I want to tell you something.

36
04:56.319 --> 04:56.920
Listen...

37
04:57.680 --> 04:58.120
Well...

38
04:58.480 --> 04:59.000
It's just...

39
04:59.800 --> 05:01.120
There's one thing I just don't get.

40
05:01.639 --> 05:03.480
Why interview me?

41
05:03.920 --> 05:05.680
I mean, all those model workers,

42
05:05.759 --> 05:06.959
and big shots in our plant, there are so many.

43
05:07.199 --> 05:08.199
Tons of them are way better than me.

44
05:08.199 --> 05:09.240
I'm nothing special.

45
05:11.000 --> 05:12.040
You're quite special.

46
05:12.800 --> 05:13.759
You just haven't realized it.

47
05:14.360 --> 05:14.800
Me?

48
05:15.120 --> 05:16.279
Besides eating a lot,

49
05:16.279 --> 05:17.319
I don't have anything special about me.

50
05:18.480 --> 05:20.000
When I filmed your plant meeting,

51
05:20.199 --> 05:22.120
you were the only one writing in a notebook.

52
05:25.800 --> 05:26.319
Oh, I see.

53
05:27.279 --> 05:28.079
I'll keep filming, then.

54
05:28.639 --> 05:29.360
Go ahead, shoot away.

55
05:29.560 --> 05:30.639
Um, should I climb back up?

56
05:30.920 --> 05:31.279
Go ahead.

57
05:32.120 --> 05:32.600
All right.

58
05:40.120 --> 05:40.600
Looking good.

59
05:41.480 --> 05:41.959
Yeah!

60
05:55.120 --> 05:55.879
Hello?

61
05:56.399 --> 05:57.480
The money's ready.

62
05:57.800 --> 05:58.439
Cash.

63
05:58.759 --> 06:00.639
Under the Qianjin Road overpass,

64
06:00.800 --> 06:01.639
100 meters north.

65
06:02.120 --> 06:02.920
Two o'clock.

66
06:04.360 --> 06:05.160
Don't be late.

67
06:05.639 --> 06:06.279
Got it.

68
08:20.519 --> 08:21.120
Where's my money?

69
08:34.480 --> 08:35.679
My name is Cheng Youtian.

70
08:36.519 --> 08:38.000
Head of the bottling workshop.

71
08:38.159 --> 08:38.759
Cheng Youtian.

72
08:39.240 --> 08:40.840
I've worked here for 25 years.

73
08:42.080 --> 08:43.519
Lacheng Beer is my home,

74
08:44.039 --> 08:45.639
and everyone loves it.

75
08:46.399 --> 08:46.919
How's that?

76
08:47.360 --> 08:48.120
That was great.

77
08:48.759 --> 08:49.759
Say a bit more.

78
08:50.720 --> 08:52.080
What else would you like to say?

79
08:54.799 --> 08:55.919
These rascals...

80
08:56.240 --> 08:57.279
are all like sons to me.

81
08:57.960 --> 08:58.679
They say

82
08:59.320 --> 09:00.960
they'll take care of me when I'm old.

83
09:01.639 --> 09:02.879
Like hell I believe that!

84
09:03.799 --> 09:04.639
Can I say that?

85
09:04.879 --> 09:05.440
Sure, sure.

86
09:05.440 --> 09:06.720
Say whatever you want.

87
09:08.120 --> 09:08.480
Come on, come on.

88
09:08.480 --> 09:09.039
Tieping.

89
09:09.279 --> 09:09.840
Master, I...

90
09:09.840 --> 09:10.440
I don't care.

91
09:10.559 --> 09:11.320
Be good, come here.

92
09:14.879 --> 09:15.519
Speak louder.

93
09:16.039 --> 09:16.480
It's fine.

94
09:21.600 --> 09:22.799
I'm too shy.

95
09:22.960 --> 09:23.679
Let the leadership speak.

96
09:29.840 --> 09:31.639
In the vibrant pulse of the city,

97
09:31.919 --> 09:33.919
Lacheng Brewery stands quietly,

98
09:34.200 --> 09:37.080
like a temple brewing dreams and passion.

99
09:37.279 --> 09:38.440
Director Ma Guowen,

100
09:38.440 --> 09:39.759
a leader who has dedicated many years

101
09:39.759 --> 09:41.240
to the beer industry,

102
09:41.240 --> 09:43.840
with his vision and bold decisions,

103
09:43.840 --> 09:46.159
has guided the path for Lacheng Brewery.

104
09:46.159 --> 09:48.480
He knows quality is the company's lifeline.

105
09:48.679 --> 09:50.279
Every market insight,

106
09:50.279 --> 09:51.840
every strategic plan,

107
09:51.960 --> 09:54.799
is filled with boundless passion for beer.

108
09:55.399 --> 09:57.200
Chief Engineer Chen Qingchun,

109
09:57.200 --> 09:59.519
with over 30 years of frontline experience,

110
10:00.000 --> 10:01.240
holds his craft to the highest standards,

111
10:01.440 --> 10:02.759
constantly striving for perfection.

112
10:09.919 --> 10:10.840
Chen Qingchun.

113
10:11.840 --> 10:12.919
That Ma Guowen...

114
10:13.360 --> 10:14.039
came to see me.

115
10:15.320 --> 10:17.240
He wants me to join him.

116
10:18.399 --> 10:19.320
He even told me

117
10:20.960 --> 10:22.559
that auctioning off the brewery

118
10:23.080 --> 10:23.720
takes two million.

119
10:24.200 --> 10:24.840
Once he flips it,

120
10:25.440 --> 10:26.039
he'll get it right back.

121
10:27.600 --> 10:28.159
Think about it.

122
10:28.320 --> 10:29.240
Two million!

123
10:30.360 --> 10:31.440
Where is he getting that money?

124
10:31.720 --> 10:32.200
You tell me.

125
10:32.879 --> 10:33.519
Right, right, right.

126
10:36.080 --> 10:37.559
Isn't he pooling money?

127
10:38.600 --> 10:39.440
So that's why I say,

128
10:39.919 --> 10:41.440
we need to pool our money too!

129
10:41.759 --> 10:42.440
Right, right!

130
10:42.600 --> 10:43.000
Right!

131
10:43.960 --> 10:46.000
If we can just raise a quarter of it,

132
10:46.720 --> 10:47.519
500,000,

133
10:48.360 --> 10:50.879
we'll have an entry ticket to the auction!

134
10:52.320 --> 10:53.759
There are dozens,

135
10:54.320 --> 10:55.080
hundreds

136
10:56.080 --> 10:57.279
of brothers and sisters among us.

137
10:57.919 --> 10:59.600
If we all pull together,

138
10:59.840 --> 11:01.720
we'll have the capital

139
11:02.320 --> 11:04.240
to fight Ma Guowen to the death!

140
11:06.039 --> 11:06.440
Now,

141
11:08.559 --> 11:09.639
here's my pledge today:

142
11:11.320 --> 11:11.840
50,000.

143
11:35.559 --> 11:36.480
If you ask me,

144
11:37.720 --> 11:39.080
Lao Chen has a point.

145
11:40.240 --> 11:41.039
Either way,

146
11:41.399 --> 11:43.240
lately, whenever I think about the factory

147
11:43.759 --> 11:44.919
being ours from now on,

148
11:45.480 --> 11:46.240
I get so excited.

149
12:00.159 --> 12:00.679
Anyone else?

150
12:08.679 --> 12:09.320
Holy smokes!

151
12:10.360 --> 12:11.159
Look at him go!

152
12:11.360 --> 12:12.080
Anyone else?

153
12:13.039 --> 12:13.639
Um...

154
12:14.039 --> 12:15.840
I only have 500 on me today.

155
12:16.000 --> 12:17.120
I'll put in this much for now.

156
12:17.639 --> 12:18.360
As for the rest...

157
12:18.399 --> 12:19.360
I'll go back and fetch it for you.

158
12:20.799 --> 12:21.639
You gotta admit...

159
12:22.120 --> 12:24.720
Cao Jun's attitude is exactly what we need.

160
12:25.039 --> 12:26.360
Come on, write him down.

161
12:26.559 --> 12:27.039
500.

162
12:27.320 --> 12:28.120
Put down 500 for now.

163
12:28.320 --> 12:28.840
Okay.

164
12:29.039 --> 12:29.480
Right, right.

165
12:29.559 --> 12:30.279
Write it down for him.

166
12:30.360 --> 12:31.200
I've got 100 here.

167
12:31.919 --> 12:32.720
Put me down first.

168
12:37.159 --> 12:37.840
I've got some too.

169
12:39.759 --> 12:40.519
Chunyan, write it down.

170
12:40.519 --> 12:41.120
Here's mine.

171
12:41.120 --> 12:41.960
Got 400 here.

172
12:42.360 --> 12:43.080
Wait, hold on.

173
12:43.080 --> 12:43.559
Write it down in a second.

174
12:43.639 --> 12:44.320
Chuan, Chuan!

175
12:44.320 --> 12:44.919
Lend me 200.

176
12:46.000 --> 12:46.480
How much?

177
12:46.840 --> 12:47.519
200. Put me down for it!

178
12:47.600 --> 12:48.039
200.

179
12:48.120 --> 12:48.559
Wait!

180
12:49.320 --> 12:50.440
Lend me 100 too!

181
12:52.200 --> 12:52.960
125.

182
12:53.480 --> 12:54.159
One... 100.

183
12:55.480 --> 12:56.519
From me and Tieping.

184
12:57.440 --> 12:57.919
Chunyan!

185
12:58.120 --> 12:59.080
Me too, Chunyan!

186
12:59.200 --> 12:59.720
Tieping.

187
12:59.960 --> 13:00.600
110.

188
13:00.679 --> 13:01.159
Ge Shun.

189
13:01.159 --> 13:01.919
Ge Shun, 100.

190
13:01.919 --> 13:02.600
Slow down, everyone.

191
13:02.639 --> 13:03.240
Slow down, slow down.

192
13:03.320 --> 13:04.000
One at a time!

193
13:04.159 --> 13:04.480
Take it easy.

194
13:04.480 --> 13:05.000
Take it easy, I'll go get the rest!

195
13:05.080 --> 13:05.840
One at a time!

196
13:06.519 --> 13:07.080
Here, here...

197
13:07.320 --> 13:07.840
What's this?

198
13:08.559 --> 13:08.919
Hold on.

199
13:09.200 --> 13:09.720
Don't be so stingy.

200
13:09.720 --> 13:10.840
Okay, I've got you all down.

201
13:11.159 --> 13:12.440
Add two more yuan for Shunzi.

202
13:12.559 --> 13:13.559
Here's ten yuan.

203
13:13.840 --> 13:14.840
Here, here, here.

204
13:15.039 --> 13:15.519
Sun Jianguo, seven yuan. Let's just...

205
13:15.519 --> 13:16.480
Just call it 15.

206
13:16.840 --> 13:17.639
The amount doesn't matter.

207
13:17.679 --> 13:18.480
It's the thought that counts.

208
13:20.639 --> 13:21.399
Shunzi, nine yuan.

209
13:21.440 --> 13:21.919
Seven yuan.

210
13:21.919 --> 13:22.480
I'll add one yuan.

211
13:23.000 --> 13:24.000
Who pitches in seven yuan?

212
13:24.080 --> 13:24.600
Nine yuan.

213
13:25.960 --> 13:26.600
Come on, come on.

214
13:26.679 --> 13:27.000
Come on, now.

215
13:27.039 --> 13:27.559
Here, here, here.

216
13:28.320 --> 13:28.879
Don't crowd!

217
13:28.960 --> 13:29.519
Listen to Chunyan!

218
13:30.080 --> 13:31.320
Alright, anyone else?

219
13:31.519 --> 13:32.000
Anyone else?

220
13:34.799 --> 13:35.200
Yeah!

221
13:35.600 --> 13:36.320
Yeah, yeah!

222
14:09.840 --> 14:10.679
At 7:30 this morning,

223
14:11.039 --> 14:12.679
a worker from Lacheng Brewery called it in.

224
14:12.960 --> 14:14.519
He said this three-wheeler belongs to Cao Jun.

225
14:14.840 --> 14:15.679
Preliminary examination shows

226
14:15.799 --> 14:17.399
the victim died of asphyxiation.

227
14:17.840 --> 14:18.799
Time of death

228
14:18.799 --> 14:20.080
was between 2:00 and 2:30 a.m.

229
14:20.080 --> 14:20.840
No injuries on this side, right?

230
14:20.840 --> 14:23.120
Multiple strike marks on the head,

231
14:23.600 --> 14:24.960
likely caused by a blunt object.

232
14:25.200 --> 14:26.399
There are ligature marks on the neck as well.

233
14:27.000 --> 14:28.559
The killer is most likely male.

234
14:29.120 --> 14:29.759
Done.

235
14:29.759 --> 14:30.879
Bottle caps again.

236
14:31.799 --> 14:32.600
And a black plastic bag.

237
14:34.320 --> 14:35.000
Cao Jun...

238
14:36.000 --> 14:37.080
We just questioned him,

239
14:37.080 --> 14:38.480
and now he's been murdered.

240
14:40.919 --> 14:42.320
Talk about brazen.

241
14:42.919 --> 14:43.480
Captain Han,

242
14:43.840 --> 14:45.919
can we strongly suspect

243
14:46.080 --> 14:47.000
a serial killer?

244
14:48.279 --> 14:49.440
They're taunting us.

245
14:51.519 --> 14:53.639
Pull all of Cao Jun's call logs.

246
14:53.759 --> 14:55.200
Especially right before he died.

247
14:56.240 --> 14:56.679
Yes, sir.

248
14:58.960 --> 14:59.639
Where's Gao Xuelin?

249
15:00.240 --> 15:01.879
He went to the old factory area.

250
15:53.000 --> 15:53.440
Pull over!

251
15:54.240 --> 15:54.799
Stop, stop, stop!

252
15:55.360 --> 15:55.960
What's your business?

253
15:56.360 --> 15:57.159
Park by the curb.

254
15:57.279 --> 15:58.080
Get out and sign in.

255
15:58.200 --> 15:59.200
I'm heading to Workshop One.

256
15:59.360 --> 16:01.159
Whichever workshop it is, you gotta sign in.

257
16:01.360 --> 16:02.159
What's his problem?

258
16:02.279 --> 16:03.240
Cocky bastard.

259
16:03.840 --> 16:04.559
Get out and sign in.

260
16:06.039 --> 16:06.679
Who knows?

261
16:06.720 --> 16:07.360
Giving me attitude.

262
16:07.399 --> 16:07.759
Where's he from?

263
16:07.840 --> 16:08.679
Workshop One, my ass.

264
16:08.679 --> 16:09.440
Never seen him before.

265
16:10.159 --> 16:11.080
Lacheng Criminal Police.

266
16:11.559 --> 16:11.960
Holy crap!

267
16:12.320 --> 16:13.320
Even the detectives are here.

268
16:13.720 --> 16:15.039
What happened to our plant?

269
16:15.679 --> 16:16.360
This... this...

270
16:16.360 --> 16:17.279
Someone hit the statue.

271
16:17.279 --> 16:18.840
And Cao Jun was strangled to death.

272
16:19.600 --> 16:20.440
The statue got smashed.

273
16:20.879 --> 16:21.759
It got rammed right here.

274
16:21.759 --> 16:22.200
Look.

275
16:22.200 --> 16:22.960
Take a look here.

276
16:23.399 --> 16:24.200
Who hit the statue?

277
16:25.279 --> 16:26.399
Our plant's former chief engineer.

278
16:26.480 --> 16:27.399
Name's Chen Qingchun.

279
16:27.519 --> 16:28.279
He came by early this morning...

280
16:28.399 --> 16:28.960
...saying he hit it.

281
16:29.000 --> 16:29.960
Then Traffic Police took him away.

282
16:31.200 --> 16:31.799
When was it hit?

283
16:32.120 --> 16:32.639
Last night.

284
16:32.919 --> 16:33.320
In the middle of the night.

285
16:33.799 --> 16:35.519
I was fast asleep, having a sweet dream.

286
16:35.639 --> 16:36.480
Then BAM!

287
16:36.600 --> 16:37.799
I thought someone crashed into my bed.

288
16:38.240 --> 16:38.679
Captain Han.

289
16:39.919 --> 16:42.159
Wasn't midnight Cao Jun's time of death?

290
16:45.600 --> 16:46.480
Did he hit it on purpose,

291
16:46.480 --> 16:47.200
or was it an accident?

292
16:47.679 --> 16:48.519
How would I know?

293
16:48.519 --> 16:49.240
I'm just a security guard.

294
16:49.279 --> 16:50.399
That's not my call.

295
16:50.480 --> 16:51.559
That's for the traffic cops.

296
16:52.120 --> 16:52.799
Were you on duty last night?

297
16:53.080 --> 16:53.600
Yes, I was.

298
16:55.600 --> 16:56.559
Can I drive the car in?

299
16:56.759 --> 16:57.240
Sure, sure.

300
16:57.240 --> 16:57.799
Yeah, you can.

301
16:57.840 --> 16:58.679
I... I can drive it for you.

302
16:58.759 --> 16:59.200
No need.

303
16:59.799 --> 17:00.279
Don't trust me?

304
17:00.759 --> 17:02.320
Cut the crap.

305
17:02.679 --> 17:03.440
I'm actually a decent driver.

306
17:03.720 --> 17:04.599
How do I get to Workshop One?

307
17:05.759 --> 17:06.880
Go inside, head in and take a left.

308
17:07.279 --> 17:07.559
Okay.

309
17:07.880 --> 17:08.759
Take... take it slow!

310
17:09.079 --> 17:10.039
Hey, hey!

311
17:10.160 --> 17:11.119
A gray Jetta!

312
17:11.119 --> 17:11.880
Letting one in!

313
17:15.240 --> 17:16.559
What are you doing taking a stroll here?

314
17:18.799 --> 17:19.359
A stroll?

315
17:19.960 --> 17:21.200
Someone just died around here.

316
17:21.400 --> 17:22.839
Who'd come here for a stroll?

317
17:24.559 --> 17:25.359
Good that you know.

318
17:25.880 --> 17:27.119
Don't get in the way of official business.

319
17:27.599 --> 17:28.519
Who are you kidding?

320
17:28.759 --> 17:29.799
Official business?

321
17:30.039 --> 17:31.440
You wouldn't be all by yourself.

322
17:32.079 --> 17:33.359
My partner's right nearby.

323
17:35.119 --> 17:36.519
The one stalking me these past few days...

324
17:36.839 --> 17:37.920
It wasn't you, was it?

325
17:38.720 --> 17:39.720
I'm not a creep.

326
17:40.200 --> 17:41.079
Why would I stalk you?

327
17:49.160 --> 17:50.920
I was wondering why you picked this spot.

328
17:52.240 --> 17:53.920
There isn't even a camera around.

329
17:54.960 --> 17:56.200
You don't look that old,

330
17:56.960 --> 17:58.279
but you're quite calculating.

331
17:59.599 --> 18:00.279
Coincidence.

332
18:01.359 --> 18:02.039
Just a coincidence.

333
18:05.920 --> 18:07.759
Since we ran into each other,

334
18:08.160 --> 18:08.839
let's chat.

335
18:09.960 --> 18:11.680
Tell me old stories about Lacheng Brewery.

336
18:12.240 --> 18:13.359
There are plenty of old stories.

337
18:14.160 --> 18:15.400
Which part do you want to hear, Officer Gao?

338
18:16.720 --> 18:17.519
Liu Xuemei.

339
18:23.720 --> 18:24.559
Yesterday,

340
18:24.759 --> 18:26.559
I watched your "Malt Kingdom" a few times.

341
18:26.960 --> 18:27.559
It was good.

342
18:29.079 --> 18:30.200
But I have a question

343
18:31.039 --> 18:32.319
for Director Shen.

344
18:34.920 --> 18:36.240
Back when you were filming,

345
18:36.240 --> 18:37.960
there was a beer taster named Liu Xuemei

346
18:38.440 --> 18:38.920
who froze to death.

347
18:39.599 --> 18:40.680
On Millennium Eve.

348
18:41.480 --> 18:43.400
It was big news in Lacheng back then.

349
18:43.720 --> 18:44.799
It was even on TV.

350
18:46.319 --> 18:47.799
You were the one who interviewed her, right?

351
18:48.640 --> 18:49.279
Yet I

352
18:49.640 --> 18:51.400
didn't see her in "Malt Kingdom."

353
18:51.960 --> 18:52.880
Not a single mention,

354
18:53.039 --> 18:54.279
not even a single shot.

355
18:54.559 --> 18:55.000
Why?

356
18:55.839 --> 18:57.480
There were lots of people at the brewery.

357
18:58.079 --> 18:59.319
Not everyone

358
18:59.480 --> 19:00.920
made it into the documentary.

359
19:02.359 --> 19:03.480
Did you interview her, then?

360
19:04.200 --> 19:05.000
I did.

361
19:05.359 --> 19:06.400
Then why wasn't she in it?

362
19:06.759 --> 19:07.640
Didn't I just tell you?

363
19:07.640 --> 19:08.519
There were lots of people.

364
19:08.519 --> 19:09.720
Not everyone was included.

365
19:11.640 --> 19:13.680
You were there the day Ma Guowen bid on the plant, right?

366
19:14.359 --> 19:15.160
Was Liu Xuemei there?

367
19:15.759 --> 19:16.799
Did anything happen?

368
19:19.039 --> 19:20.000
No comment.

369
19:22.160 --> 19:23.039
Your documentary

370
19:23.039 --> 19:25.000
hid a lot of the truth back then.

371
19:25.480 --> 19:26.839
How did Qian Yichuan's leg get crippled?

372
19:27.319 --> 19:29.799
Cheng Youtian, Tu Chunyan, Cao Jun,

373
19:30.720 --> 19:31.480
Zhao Haipeng...

374
19:31.759 --> 19:32.960
How did they all end up laid off?

375
19:33.599 --> 19:35.160
Was it because they wanted to bid on the plant

376
19:35.160 --> 19:36.160
and crossed Ma Guowen?

377
19:36.400 --> 19:37.279
Liu Xuemei's death...

378
19:37.279 --> 19:38.400
did it have anything to do with this?

379
19:45.799 --> 19:47.359
I'd like to ask you something too, Officer Gao.

380
19:48.400 --> 19:49.960
What is Liu Xuemei to you?

381
19:50.359 --> 19:51.720
Why do you care so much about her?

382
19:52.880 --> 19:53.920
I know she had a son.

383
19:54.319 --> 19:55.359
He was seven or eight back then,

384
19:56.039 --> 19:57.359
around your age.

385
20:09.640 --> 20:10.400
Not answering

386
20:10.960 --> 20:11.640
means you're admitting it.

387
20:13.960 --> 20:15.200
What you just said

388
20:15.559 --> 20:17.319
doesn't sound like recent findings.

389
20:18.039 --> 20:20.920
It sounds more like

390
20:21.160 --> 20:23.039
you started watching these people long ago.

391
20:23.880 --> 20:25.319
I don't need to tell you my business.

392
20:26.480 --> 20:28.359
Answer my question directly.

393
20:29.319 --> 20:30.759
Why should I answer you?

394
20:31.359 --> 20:32.559
Am I a suspect?

395
20:33.599 --> 20:35.480
You haven't solved Ma Guowen's death,

396
20:35.880 --> 20:37.119
and now you're grilling me about Liu Xuemei.

397
20:37.720 --> 20:38.960
Go do your actual job.

398
20:40.039 --> 20:40.680
Stop right there.

399
20:42.440 --> 20:44.319
What really happened the day Liu Xuemei died?

400
20:44.319 --> 20:45.519
You definitely shot footage.

401
20:46.039 --> 20:46.880
Give me the footage.

402
20:47.440 --> 20:48.480
I don't have it.

403
20:48.680 --> 20:50.400
You just said you interviewed her.

404
20:51.039 --> 20:52.200
Where's the unused footage from back then?

405
20:52.880 --> 20:53.799
Why are you afraid to show it?

406
20:54.759 --> 20:55.799
You've crossed the line.

407
21:08.839 --> 21:10.079
Who are you really?

408
21:11.759 --> 21:13.599
What's your connection to Liu Xuemei?

409
21:15.119 --> 21:17.079
You don't care about what you should be investigating,

410
21:17.519 --> 21:19.200
yet you won't leave Liu Xuemei alone.

411
21:21.720 --> 21:22.880
I should be asking you,

412
21:24.920 --> 21:26.519
what's your deal?

413
21:53.319 --> 21:54.319
Go call him over for me.

414
21:54.599 --> 21:55.119
Sure.

415
21:55.119 --> 21:55.799
Thanks.

416
22:08.039 --> 22:09.359
You're Liu Tieping, right?

417
22:10.319 --> 22:12.200
We're from the Lacheng Criminal Investigation Detachment.

418
22:12.799 --> 22:13.920
Since you reported the crime,

419
22:14.200 --> 22:15.480
I need to ask you a few questions.

420
22:15.640 --> 22:16.799
This is Officer Han Chuang.

421
22:17.279 --> 22:17.880
Hello.

422
22:19.000 --> 22:20.440
You're pretty dedicated to your job.

423
22:21.319 --> 22:22.000
The factory director is dead,

424
22:22.000 --> 22:23.000
the plant is being sold off,

425
22:23.119 --> 22:24.839
and a lot of workers stopped showing up.

426
22:25.359 --> 22:26.680
Yet you're still here working.

427
22:30.240 --> 22:30.960
So,

428
22:31.440 --> 22:32.920
let me ask you a few things.

429
22:34.640 --> 22:37.119
The plant is over ten kilometers from the scene.

430
22:37.119 --> 22:39.200
How did you find Cao Jun's body?

431
22:40.440 --> 22:41.920
I passed by on my way to work.

432
22:42.799 --> 22:43.720
Where do you live?

433
22:44.440 --> 22:45.599
The west tenement building.

434
22:46.799 --> 22:48.160
The west tenement building.

435
22:50.480 --> 22:52.880
What were you doing last night after ten?

436
22:55.559 --> 22:56.400
I was drinking.

437
22:57.279 --> 22:58.359
Where were you drinking?

438
23:00.960 --> 23:01.960
Just in my dorm.

439
23:03.440 --> 23:04.440
Who were you drinking with?

440
23:06.799 --> 23:07.359
Li San.

441
23:08.920 --> 23:09.680
That's him right there.

442
23:11.559 --> 23:12.319
Go over and ask him.

443
23:16.319 --> 23:18.319
How late were you drinking last night?

444
23:22.079 --> 23:22.680
Don't know.

445
23:24.240 --> 23:25.319
Then how much did you drink?

446
23:36.240 --> 23:36.960
I don't know.

447
23:39.079 --> 23:40.160
What time did you wake up?

448
23:42.160 --> 23:44.160
I... I went to work as soon as I woke up.

449
23:46.480 --> 23:48.839
Then how did you find Cao Jun's body this morning?

450
23:50.319 --> 23:51.559
I just passed by on my way to work.

451
23:54.440 --> 23:55.119
And then?

452
23:58.480 --> 23:58.839
I... I...

453
23:58.839 --> 24:01.160
Mostly, I just noticed his car.

454
24:01.839 --> 24:03.440
You recognize Cao Jun's car, right?

455
24:04.440 --> 24:05.599
You recognized that car.

456
24:11.240 --> 24:12.480
Think back.

457
24:13.279 --> 24:15.759
Who in the factory had bad blood

458
24:15.960 --> 24:17.319
with Ma Guowen and Cao Jun?

459
24:24.759 --> 24:26.960
How many years have you known Ma Guowen and Cao Jun?

460
24:30.799 --> 24:32.839
They were already there when I joined the factory.

461
24:35.799 --> 24:37.279
How many years have you been at the factory?

462
24:39.799 --> 24:40.839
Around ten years, I guess.

463
24:44.279 --> 24:45.519
Then think about it.

464
24:45.839 --> 24:47.680
Normally, who was

465
24:47.920 --> 24:49.400
on good terms with Ma Guowen?

466
25:04.200 --> 25:05.720
Who was close to Cao Jun?

467
25:12.839 --> 25:13.759
Haven't sobered up yet?

468
25:15.519 --> 25:16.240
I'm sober.

469
25:16.640 --> 25:17.319
I'm working.

470
25:19.559 --> 25:20.119
All right.

471
25:20.559 --> 25:21.079
Look.

472
25:22.279 --> 25:23.640
I'll give you my number.

473
25:24.680 --> 25:25.440
Here's my number.

474
25:25.519 --> 25:26.240
My name's Han.

475
25:27.880 --> 25:28.799
When your head clears up,

476
25:28.799 --> 25:29.680
if you remember anything,

477
25:29.720 --> 25:30.559
give me a call.

478
25:30.599 --> 25:31.200
Okay?

479
25:34.039 --> 25:34.799
Drink less.

480
25:35.240 --> 25:36.000
It rots your brain.

481
25:41.400 --> 25:42.160
Tech investigated.

482
25:42.680 --> 25:44.400
The last call made to Cao Jun

483
25:44.400 --> 25:45.359
was from an unregistered SIM card.

484
25:45.839 --> 25:47.319
So that lead is dead.

485
25:47.759 --> 25:48.119
Right.

486
25:48.559 --> 25:49.400
Cao Jun died last night

487
25:49.400 --> 25:51.319
between two and two-thirty, right?

488
25:51.640 --> 25:52.119
That guy? Yeah.

489
25:52.119 --> 25:54.160
The body was found this morning.

490
25:54.440 --> 25:56.160
Last night at ten,

491
25:56.759 --> 25:58.839
he was drinking with friends until two.

492
25:59.279 --> 26:00.759
What time was the statue at the gate hit?

493
26:00.960 --> 26:02.640
A little after two in the morning.

494
26:04.519 --> 26:05.680
The crime scene

495
26:05.920 --> 26:07.440
is over ten kilometers from the factory.

496
26:08.519 --> 26:10.079
It couldn't be Chen Qingchun either.

497
26:10.319 --> 26:11.119
It's too far.

498
26:11.400 --> 26:11.920
Impossible.

499
26:12.960 --> 26:14.599
Your mind sure works fast.

500
26:15.039 --> 26:16.599
Jumping all over the place.

501
26:16.799 --> 26:17.640
Is Gao back yet?

502
26:18.119 --> 26:19.319
I've been busy all morning.

503
26:19.400 --> 26:20.640
Who's got time to check on him?

504
26:24.920 --> 26:25.279
Over here.

505
26:25.359 --> 26:25.960
Cai.

506
26:27.920 --> 26:28.480
You're up so early.

507
26:28.519 --> 26:29.279
What are you having?

508
26:30.039 --> 26:30.759
Boss,

509
26:31.640 --> 26:32.480
a bowl of beef noodles.

510
26:32.640 --> 26:33.400
Sure thing, just a moment.

511
26:34.000 --> 26:35.720
I thought people in our line of work were night owls

512
26:35.720 --> 26:36.640
who slept in.

513
26:38.000 --> 26:39.519
How did that inquiry go?

514
26:39.839 --> 26:41.319
I was just about to report to you.

515
26:41.839 --> 26:42.440
Let me tell you,

516
26:42.440 --> 26:43.119
it's such a coincidence.

517
26:43.599 --> 26:44.440
He's from Qingzhou.

518
26:44.680 --> 26:45.599
I'm from Qingzhou too.

519
26:45.759 --> 26:47.200
And we went to the same middle school.

520
26:47.440 --> 26:48.279
He was two grades below me,

521
26:48.279 --> 26:49.039
so I didn't know him.

522
26:49.759 --> 26:51.759
But I know some of his classmates.

523
26:52.079 --> 26:53.119
So where he lives,

524
26:53.119 --> 26:54.000
who he's closest to...

525
26:54.079 --> 26:55.039
I found it all out.

526
26:56.160 --> 26:57.759
I'll send the info to your phone.

527
26:57.799 --> 26:58.319
Okay.

528
27:02.160 --> 27:02.759
Chuang!

529
27:03.119 --> 27:03.640
Cai!

530
27:04.160 --> 27:05.319
I'm done checking the old factory area.

531
27:05.799 --> 27:07.400
Brought you guys some breakfast too.

532
27:07.640 --> 27:08.359
The steamed buns are still piping hot.

533
27:08.359 --> 27:08.920
Have some.

534
27:08.920 --> 27:09.559
Look what time it is.

535
27:09.559 --> 27:10.599
Breakfast now?

536
27:26.160 --> 27:26.720
So what?

537
27:28.359 --> 27:29.039
How many beers I drink,

538
27:29.039 --> 27:29.920
am I supposed to count?

539
27:30.799 --> 27:31.640
I smoke too.

540
27:32.799 --> 27:34.119
How many cigarettes I smoke a day,

541
27:34.799 --> 27:35.599
how would I remember?

542
27:36.839 --> 27:39.279
What time did you last see Cao Jun last night?

543
27:41.359 --> 27:41.960
Past eight, I guess.

544
27:42.640 --> 27:43.519
Where did you see him?

545
27:44.319 --> 27:45.400
Downstairs by the trash.

546
27:45.880 --> 27:46.799
Did you say anything to each other?

547
27:49.759 --> 27:50.680
Didn't say a thing.

548
27:52.799 --> 27:54.000
Are you and Cao Jun close?

549
27:56.200 --> 27:56.720
Not close.

550
27:58.119 --> 27:58.799
Not close?

551
27:59.480 --> 28:01.720
Weren't you coworkers at the old Lacheng Brewery?

552
28:02.480 --> 28:03.480
How could you not be close?

553
28:08.200 --> 28:09.559
Our entire building

554
28:09.720 --> 28:11.079
worked at the old Lacheng Brewery.

555
28:11.720 --> 28:12.680
That's dozens of families.

556
28:13.680 --> 28:14.880
Am I supposed to know everyone?

557
28:16.200 --> 28:17.000
Think about it.

558
28:18.319 --> 28:19.319
Out of dozens of families,

559
28:19.960 --> 28:21.440
why did I single you out?

560
28:26.319 --> 28:27.240
I have no idea.

561
28:30.400 --> 28:31.480
Let me give you a hint.

562
28:33.039 --> 28:34.599
Someone said at eight last night,

563
28:34.640 --> 28:35.519
you went to Cao Jun's place.

564
28:35.559 --> 28:36.279
Is that true or not?

565
28:36.759 --> 28:37.480
Who said that?

566
28:37.759 --> 28:38.680
Never mind who.

567
28:38.720 --> 28:39.400
Did you go?

568
28:39.400 --> 28:40.079
Is it true?

569
28:41.400 --> 28:42.400
Was it Shen Leshui?

570
28:47.400 --> 28:48.880
I've got beef with her.

571
28:49.400 --> 28:51.160
I just left some stuff by her door,

572
28:51.160 --> 28:52.160
and she messes with me every day,

573
28:52.160 --> 28:53.400
snitching on me everywhere.

574
28:54.079 --> 28:54.960
That woman,

575
28:55.920 --> 28:57.359
she's just like the saying—

576
28:57.359 --> 28:58.279
nothing but a big mouth.

577
28:58.359 --> 28:59.240
You can't believe a word she says.

578
28:59.279 --> 28:59.640
That's enough.

579
28:59.640 --> 29:01.640
None of this has anything to do with the case.

580
29:01.839 --> 29:02.799
What I'm asking you right now is,

581
29:02.839 --> 29:03.799
at eight last night,

582
29:03.880 --> 29:05.200
did you go to Cao Jun's place?

583
29:05.599 --> 29:06.559
Think carefully.

584
29:07.400 --> 29:07.920
This

585
29:07.960 --> 29:09.960
is vital to both the victim, Cao Jun, and you.

586
29:15.640 --> 29:16.400
I went.

587
29:17.240 --> 29:18.200
But we didn't do anything.

588
29:18.480 --> 29:19.279
Didn't do anything?

589
29:20.119 --> 29:21.359
Think carefully before you speak.

590
29:22.079 --> 29:23.000
You go to his home,

591
29:23.279 --> 29:24.039
do nothing at all—

592
29:24.759 --> 29:25.559
then what did you go for?

593
29:27.559 --> 29:28.440
He asked me over.

594
29:29.519 --> 29:30.400
To do what?

595
29:34.039 --> 29:34.720
Sleep together.

596
29:35.319 --> 29:36.640
Didn't you say you weren't close?

597
29:37.240 --> 29:38.839
You chat a bit and get close, right?

598
29:39.920 --> 29:40.759
What's the problem?

599
29:41.240 --> 29:42.160
He has no wife,

600
29:43.319 --> 29:44.200
and I have no husband.

601
29:45.240 --> 29:46.920
Can't the two of us sleep together?

602
29:53.400 --> 29:53.960
You can.

603
29:54.400 --> 29:55.240
I didn't say you couldn't.

604
29:55.799 --> 29:56.599
Then why ask?

605
29:57.400 --> 29:58.240
All the more reason to ask.

606
29:58.920 --> 30:00.279
What state was Cao Jun in that night?

607
30:01.079 --> 30:02.160
What do you mean, "what state"?

608
30:03.279 --> 30:04.599
You want details?

609
30:07.880 --> 30:08.440
Fine.

610
30:10.920 --> 30:11.720
Cao Jun—

611
30:12.319 --> 30:13.200
who was he close to?

612
30:14.759 --> 30:15.359
Don't know.

613
30:15.920 --> 30:17.680
Who did Cao Jun have bad blood with?

614
30:20.279 --> 30:20.960
Don't know.

615
30:21.319 --> 30:22.720
Fine. Playing dumb on everything, huh?

616
30:24.119 --> 30:24.720
Tu Chunyan.

617
30:25.200 --> 30:25.960
Let me tell you something.

618
30:26.440 --> 30:27.839
As far as we know,

619
30:28.119 --> 30:29.880
you were the last person to see Cao Jun yesterday,

620
30:30.279 --> 30:32.000
and you two had intimate contact.

621
30:32.759 --> 30:34.359
I hope you'll cooperate,

622
30:34.400 --> 30:36.200
and tell me everything you know.

623
30:36.720 --> 30:38.359
Otherwise, once you walk out that door,

624
30:39.079 --> 30:40.000
I'm going to investigate you.

625
30:41.079 --> 30:42.279
Want to make a bet?

626
30:42.720 --> 30:43.920
I can dig up every single thing

627
30:43.960 --> 30:44.839
you've ever done.

628
30:45.519 --> 30:46.640
When I haul you back in,

629
30:46.640 --> 30:47.400
things will be very different.

630
30:47.640 --> 30:48.599
Weigh your options.

631
31:15.079 --> 31:15.839
Cao Jun...

632
31:17.599 --> 31:18.960
has a habit of keeping a diary.

633
31:20.960 --> 31:22.680
There's a diary under his pillow.

634
31:23.279 --> 31:24.920
He wrote all kinds of weird things in it.

635
31:25.880 --> 31:26.759
I didn't really get it.

636
31:27.400 --> 31:28.559
If you want to know,

637
31:29.400 --> 31:30.920
go take a look at it yourself.

638
31:34.200 --> 31:34.960
What kind of notebook?

639
31:37.640 --> 31:39.240
A little red notebook.

640
31:40.599 --> 31:41.720
It has the word "Award" on it.

641
31:43.279 --> 31:44.359
Back in the day,

642
31:46.519 --> 31:48.440
the factory gave it to him for being a model worker.

643
31:55.000 --> 31:57.039
What time did you leave Cao Jun's place last night?

644
32:01.519 --> 32:02.440
Around nine or so.

645
32:04.680 --> 32:06.079
Once he fell asleep, I left.

646
32:10.839 --> 32:12.119
Was there money exchanged between you two?

647
32:19.559 --> 32:21.519
Was there money exchanged between you two?

648
32:22.400 --> 32:23.759
I don't make money that way.

649
32:27.880 --> 32:29.160
Cao Jun is a good man.

650
32:29.160 --> 32:30.079
You know that?

651
32:31.319 --> 32:32.759
I've known him for so many years,

652
32:33.599 --> 32:35.960
and he never once lost his temper at anyone.

653
32:36.240 --> 32:38.319
I have no idea who he could've crossed.

654
32:39.599 --> 32:41.240
Whoever killed Cao Jun,

655
32:41.920 --> 32:43.200
they'll die a miserable death!

656
32:43.599 --> 32:44.680
You cops,

657
32:44.680 --> 32:45.640
do your damn job!

658
32:45.720 --> 32:47.440
Hurry up and catch the killer!

659
32:50.440 --> 32:51.559
Please sit down first.

660
33:12.000 --> 33:12.640
I found it.

661
33:12.720 --> 33:13.079
Chuang.

662
33:13.519 --> 33:15.079
The diary from Tu Chunyan's statement.

663
33:17.680 --> 33:19.039
"Soul Massage."

664
33:19.599 --> 33:20.079
This one.

665
33:21.359 --> 33:21.960
Xiao Wu.

666
33:22.519 --> 33:23.240
Coming, Chuang.

667
33:25.119 --> 33:25.559
Here.

668
33:26.200 --> 33:27.720
Go through all the info

669
33:27.799 --> 33:28.319
in this diary.

670
33:28.480 --> 33:28.839
Got it.

671
33:28.839 --> 33:29.319
Check it thoroughly.

672
33:36.319 --> 33:37.000
Here, give it to me.

673
33:41.160 --> 33:41.839
What does this mean?

674
33:41.960 --> 33:43.480
He used to drive a forklift.

675
33:43.480 --> 33:44.279
Now he drives an auto-rickshaw.

676
33:44.279 --> 33:46.079
Why would he keep photos of scrapped cars?

677
33:51.319 --> 33:52.440
Let me see what it says.

678
33:55.240 --> 33:56.000
Touch-up paint.

679
33:56.720 --> 33:58.039
Scrapping procedure.

680
33:58.640 --> 34:01.200
Retirement age for division-level cadres.

681
34:06.559 --> 34:07.519
"I found..."

682
34:08.960 --> 34:10.360
What, you think I can't read?

683
34:14.760 --> 34:16.559
"I found the traitor who betrayed our fellow workers."

684
34:17.119 --> 34:18.800
"With leverage on him, I can turn things around."

685
34:20.079 --> 34:20.599
Traitor.

686
34:23.519 --> 34:25.159
Chuang, I think there's something off with that car.

687
34:25.559 --> 34:26.000
Xiao Wu.

688
34:26.800 --> 34:27.480
In Lacheng,

689
34:27.480 --> 34:28.960
isn't there a car scrapyard?

690
34:29.400 --> 34:29.840
Yeah.

691
34:30.679 --> 34:31.280
I know it.

692
34:31.800 --> 34:32.840
The biggest one is called

693
34:33.079 --> 34:33.679
Xinbin.

694
34:34.000 --> 34:34.719
Contact them right away,

695
34:34.719 --> 34:35.719
then send me the address.

696
34:35.920 --> 34:36.599
We'll head over soon.

697
34:38.880 --> 34:39.519
Hurry up.

698
34:43.320 --> 34:43.719
Go on.

699
34:50.800 --> 34:51.360
Chuang.

700
34:52.960 --> 34:53.840
Don't be mad anymore.

701
34:55.239 --> 34:55.960
I know I screwed up.

702
34:59.840 --> 35:00.360
Look,

703
35:00.360 --> 35:01.960
what did I tell you the other day?

704
35:03.039 --> 35:04.320
I was just so anxious.

705
35:08.119 --> 35:08.679
All right.

706
35:10.119 --> 35:10.960
Your punishment:

707
35:11.400 --> 35:12.239
buy steamed buns for three days.

708
35:12.400 --> 35:13.119
Hear me?

709
35:13.920 --> 35:15.280
I can buy them for ten days!

710
35:15.599 --> 35:16.719
I'll get you different kinds every day.

711
35:18.519 --> 35:19.039
Keep looking into it.

712
35:19.400 --> 35:19.800
Got it.

713
35:28.519 --> 35:30.079
How long have you run this scrapyard?

714
35:30.800 --> 35:31.639
Quite a while now.

715
35:33.119 --> 35:35.079
When was the last time you saw Cao Jun?

716
35:35.800 --> 35:36.800
Last week.

717
35:36.800 --> 35:37.719
On the 28th.

718
35:39.760 --> 35:40.679
You remember that pretty clearly.

719
35:41.920 --> 35:43.280
It was my birthday.

720
35:43.679 --> 35:44.920
We had a few drinks together.

721
35:45.079 --> 35:46.559
Who knew something would happen to him a few days later?

722
35:47.920 --> 35:48.559
Brothers?

723
35:48.800 --> 35:49.320
What kind of brothers?

724
35:49.360 --> 35:50.400
Are you full brothers?

725
35:51.280 --> 35:52.000
Cousin.

726
35:53.199 --> 35:53.840
Take a look.

727
35:54.599 --> 35:55.519
Does this ring a bell?

728
35:59.400 --> 36:00.239
Look familiar?

729
36:01.119 --> 36:01.679
No.

730
36:03.119 --> 36:03.760
Take a closer look.

731
36:06.559 --> 36:07.360
I really don't recognize it.

732
36:10.519 --> 36:11.079
Officers...

733
36:11.440 --> 36:12.559
Look at all the scrapped cars here.

734
36:12.559 --> 36:13.559
How could I remember every single one?

735
36:13.800 --> 36:14.320
Right?

736
36:16.559 --> 36:17.719
Then inside your cousin's diary,

737
36:17.719 --> 36:18.639
why was there a tucked-in photo

738
36:18.639 --> 36:20.599
of a scrapped car from your yard?

739
36:22.079 --> 36:23.159
How would I know?

740
36:27.239 --> 36:28.440
So it is from your yard after all.

741
36:29.159 --> 36:30.199
No, no.

742
36:30.559 --> 36:32.239
Doesn't mean it's from our yard.

743
36:32.440 --> 36:33.920
Who knows where he took it?

744
36:35.800 --> 36:38.760
Did you see Cao Jun often?

745
36:39.519 --> 36:40.639
Not really often.

746
36:40.880 --> 36:42.360
Just the occasional drink.

747
36:43.079 --> 36:43.960
What's "occasional"?

748
36:44.199 --> 36:45.280
Twice a week?

749
36:45.400 --> 36:46.360
Or twice a month?

750
36:48.480 --> 36:49.679
Hard to say.

751
36:49.719 --> 36:50.280
Just...

752
36:50.840 --> 36:52.039
Then the last time you two met,

753
36:52.239 --> 36:53.039
on your birthday,

754
36:53.039 --> 36:54.039
what did he tell you?

755
36:55.320 --> 36:56.360
I... I can't remember.

756
36:56.360 --> 36:57.519
We got wasted every time.

757
36:57.519 --> 36:58.159
Everything's a blur.

758
37:04.400 --> 37:05.360
So you don't know anything, huh?

759
37:06.599 --> 37:07.639
Total blackout.

760
37:08.239 --> 37:09.960
Did Cao Jun ever scrap a car here?

761
37:10.119 --> 37:10.639
No.

762
37:14.960 --> 37:15.679
Let me tell you something.

763
37:16.360 --> 37:18.360
We're investigating your cousin's death today.

764
37:18.480 --> 37:19.840
He was murdered.

765
37:21.159 --> 37:22.920
Can you give us any leads?

766
37:25.199 --> 37:25.920
I really don't know.

767
37:25.920 --> 37:26.519
Officers...

768
37:26.599 --> 37:26.960
I...

769
37:28.039 --> 37:29.360
my cousin was always so good to me.

770
37:29.360 --> 37:29.760
I...

771
37:30.920 --> 37:31.280
I...

772
37:31.440 --> 37:32.320
All right, I get it.

773
37:33.599 --> 37:34.679
Let me remind you, then.

774
37:35.360 --> 37:36.400
The consequences of withholding information...

775
37:37.079 --> 37:37.719
you know what they are.

776
37:40.119 --> 37:40.559
Here.

777
37:41.760 --> 37:42.519
Here's my number.

778
37:44.239 --> 37:45.920
We still hope that moving forward,

779
37:46.079 --> 37:47.400
you'll cooperate with our investigation.

780
37:47.800 --> 37:48.559
Any information,

781
37:48.559 --> 37:49.199
any leads,

782
37:49.199 --> 37:50.159
call me right away.

783
37:50.519 --> 37:50.960
Okay.

784
37:51.199 --> 37:51.920
I'll definitely cooperate.

785
37:53.000 --> 37:53.440
Let's go.

786
38:06.039 --> 38:06.559
Officer.

787
38:06.639 --> 38:07.199
Over here.

788
38:11.280 --> 38:12.119
Such a cute dog.

789
38:13.159 --> 38:13.960
Leaving it outside...

790
38:14.159 --> 38:14.960
Aren't they afraid it'll freeze?

791
38:16.079 --> 38:17.360
No idea who left it here.

792
38:19.840 --> 38:21.119
Let's get you inside, it's cold out.

793
38:21.800 --> 38:22.159
Come on.

794
38:26.039 --> 38:27.400
A cousin is close family, too.

795
38:27.920 --> 38:28.880
Why isn't he worried at all?

796
38:31.559 --> 38:32.239
There's something off about that guy.

797
38:47.159 --> 38:48.079
Stop washing it.

798
38:49.360 --> 38:50.440
Just burn it.

799
38:51.400 --> 38:52.920
Even if you scrub holes right through it,

800
38:54.440 --> 38:56.360
you won't wash away the stench of death.

801
38:57.960 --> 39:00.079
That garish red is creepy to wear anyway.

802
39:05.039 --> 39:06.760
I saw Cao Jun at Old Cheng's a couple of days ago,

803
39:06.760 --> 39:08.400
and I could tell right away something was off.

804
39:11.280 --> 39:12.239
He wasn't crying right,

805
39:12.239 --> 39:13.280
and he wasn't laughing right either.

806
39:14.639 --> 39:15.440
I'm telling you,

807
39:16.960 --> 39:18.679
when someone's about to die, it shows on their face.

808
39:33.800 --> 39:35.400
Ma Guowen had it coming.

809
39:36.920 --> 39:38.840
But who did Cao Jun piss off?

810
39:44.440 --> 39:46.320
You'd think whoever wanted Ma Guowen dead

811
39:48.079 --> 39:49.199
wouldn't kill Cao Jun.

812
39:50.360 --> 39:51.760
And whoever wanted Cao Jun dead

813
39:52.639 --> 39:54.119
definitely wouldn't kill Ma Guowen.

814
39:58.400 --> 39:59.639
Now that's interesting.

815
40:15.719 --> 40:17.400
Plus 12,000.

816
40:17.519 --> 40:18.880
Plus 3,000.

817
40:18.960 --> 40:20.280
Plus 500.

818
40:20.880 --> 40:24.199
Equals 1,996,000.

819
40:26.840 --> 40:27.599
What's wrong with you?

820
40:28.239 --> 40:29.239
What are you doing?

821
40:29.719 --> 40:30.320
What is it?

822
40:32.360 --> 40:35.800
1,996,000.

823
40:36.159 --> 40:37.079
What do you mean?

824
40:37.840 --> 40:38.800
Something's wrong.

825
40:41.880 --> 40:42.599
Just getting water.

826
40:52.400 --> 40:53.079
Are you okay?

827
40:53.800 --> 40:54.559
Something's happened.

828
40:55.280 --> 40:56.039
Stop messing around.

829
40:57.119 --> 40:57.800
Zhao Haipeng.

830
40:58.559 --> 40:59.679
We're buddies, right?

831
41:00.760 --> 41:01.440
Of course.

832
41:01.840 --> 41:02.679
Then look at me.

833
41:09.719 --> 41:10.559
What do you two want with me

834
41:10.760 --> 41:11.440
in the middle of the day?

835
41:13.440 --> 41:14.159
Talk to me.

836
41:15.320 --> 41:16.679
You've heard about the state firm restructuring, right?

837
41:17.519 --> 41:18.440
It's our factory's turn.

838
41:18.840 --> 41:20.079
Our factory is going up for auction.

839
41:20.400 --> 41:21.119
What?

840
41:26.039 --> 41:26.679
What's this?

841
41:29.320 --> 41:31.760
Ma Guowen embezzled money from our factory,

842
41:32.760 --> 41:34.360
and now he wants to use that cash

843
41:34.400 --> 41:35.880
to buy the factory for himself.

844
41:36.599 --> 41:37.000
What?

845
41:38.239 --> 41:40.119
Heard of "Smash the Old Three Irons with the New Three Irons"?

846
41:40.880 --> 41:43.199
An iron face, an iron fist, and an iron heart,

847
41:43.360 --> 41:45.440
to smash our iron armchairs, iron rice bowls, and iron wages.

848
41:47.800 --> 41:48.719
Let me put it this way.

849
41:49.199 --> 41:51.199
Once Ma Guowen buys our factory,

850
41:51.199 --> 41:52.519
we'll all become contract workers.

851
41:53.000 --> 41:54.000
If he doesn't like someone,

852
41:54.239 --> 41:55.920
he can fire them and send them packing.

853
41:56.039 --> 41:56.599
Laid off.

854
41:58.880 --> 41:59.199
No.

855
41:59.239 --> 42:00.559
Anyone Ma Guowen doesn't like,

856
42:00.559 --> 42:02.119
he can just have them laid off.

857
42:02.239 --> 42:02.880
Exactly.

858
42:03.199 --> 42:04.519
Once the factory belongs to Ma,

859
42:05.079 --> 42:06.039
all of you

860
42:06.280 --> 42:07.159
will become contract workers.

861
42:07.760 --> 42:08.440
Contract...

862
42:08.679 --> 42:09.639
Being contract workers won't do!

863
42:09.639 --> 42:10.159
If we're contract workers,

864
42:10.159 --> 42:11.400
what happens to our benefits?

865
42:11.400 --> 42:12.519
What benefits?

866
42:12.679 --> 42:13.920
A lump-sum buyout.

867
42:14.559 --> 42:15.280
They give you a pittance.

868
42:15.840 --> 42:16.599
Do you think that'll last your whole life?

869
42:17.320 --> 42:18.679
We definitely can't let that happen.

870
42:19.199 --> 42:20.039
Let me tell you this.

871
42:20.039 --> 42:20.599
Let me talk.

872
42:21.239 --> 42:21.800
Look here.

873
42:22.360 --> 42:22.800
See that?

874
42:23.320 --> 42:23.960
Ma Guowen

875
42:24.440 --> 42:27.000
not only wants to pocket state assets,

876
42:27.679 --> 42:28.960
he also wants to take all our money

877
42:29.039 --> 42:30.039
and stuff it right into his own pockets.

878
42:30.400 --> 42:31.320
Do you get it now?

879
42:31.719 --> 42:32.760
Yeah, yeah, we get it completely.

880
42:32.760 --> 42:34.119
Of course we understand.

881
42:35.159 --> 42:35.719
Can't we...

882
42:36.400 --> 42:38.000
can't we write an anonymous letter

883
42:38.280 --> 42:39.280
and report him?

884
42:39.599 --> 42:40.719
Reporting him is tricky.

885
42:42.440 --> 42:43.159
His accounting books—

886
42:43.440 --> 42:44.679
he cooked them meticulously.

887
42:45.679 --> 42:47.559
Even if we turn this in,

888
42:47.679 --> 42:49.360
it'll take forever to verify.

889
42:49.679 --> 42:50.599
By the time they're done,

890
42:50.639 --> 42:52.440
the auction will already be over.

891
42:53.559 --> 42:54.679
Buying the factory costs a fortune.

892
42:55.119 --> 42:56.320
Where would we get that kind of money?

893
42:56.480 --> 42:57.000
Yeah.

894
42:57.199 --> 42:58.199
How much money would that take?

895
42:58.480 --> 42:59.639
Just how much would we need?

896
43:00.000 --> 43:01.199
Never mind the amount for now.

897
43:01.559 --> 43:02.800
Let me break it down for you.

898
43:03.480 --> 43:05.920
To encourage corporate restructuring, the state

899
43:07.159 --> 43:08.360
sets the starting bid price

900
43:08.440 --> 43:11.320
way lower than the actual market value.

901
43:11.719 --> 43:13.320
So as long as our offer

902
43:13.400 --> 43:14.440
matches Ma Guowen's,

903
43:14.719 --> 43:16.559
they must give priority to us workers.

904
43:17.519 --> 43:19.239
We don't even know how much Ma's putting up.

905
43:20.199 --> 43:20.480
Well...

906
43:21.599 --> 43:22.280
There you are!

907
43:24.800 --> 43:26.000
Qian Yichuan has evidence.

908
43:27.199 --> 43:29.480
Ma Guowen embezzled two million from us over the years.

909
43:29.639 --> 43:30.360
Two...

910
43:31.400 --> 43:32.159
Two...

911
43:32.800 --> 43:33.639
million?!

912
43:41.360 --> 43:42.920
A black plastic bag over the head,

913
43:42.920 --> 43:44.360
clutching a beer bottle cap in the hand...

914
43:44.920 --> 43:46.679
It's the exact same way Ma Guowen died.

915
43:46.760 --> 43:47.760
When?

916
43:47.880 --> 43:48.719
I don't know.

917
43:48.840 --> 43:49.599
The way I see it,

918
43:49.880 --> 43:51.840
it's definitely the work of the same person.

919
43:52.639 --> 43:54.360
That's a serial murder case.

920
43:54.880 --> 43:56.480
Only by finding the killer as soon as possible

921
43:57.239 --> 43:59.119
can we keep anyone else from getting killed.

922
44:00.360 --> 44:02.119
You must be out of your mind!

923
44:02.800 --> 44:04.559
People are dying, and you're sticking your nose in it!
